# Project Overview

Wissenslandkarte is a web application built with Remix that serves as a knowledge mapping and project management platform.
It is created for a makerspace. Uses should be able to add projects and project steps quickly.

It allows users to:
* Create and manage projects with detailed descriptions, images, and metadata
* Organize knowledge through structured project steps and attachments
* Collaborate with team members through ownership and membership roles
* Tag and categorize content for better organization
* Search through projects and people using Meilisearch
* Support multiple languages (German and English) with i18next
* Authenticate users through Keycloak integration

# Key Features
* Project Management: Users can create projects with titles, descriptions, main images, and structured steps
* Knowledge Organization: Projects can have multiple steps with attachments and descriptions
* User Collaboration: Support for project owners and members with different permission levels
* Tagging System: Flexible tagging for both users and projects
* Metadata System: Extensible metadata types (cost, materials, time, etc.) with translations
* File Management: Attachment support for projects and project steps
* Search Functionality: Full-text search across projects and users
* Internationalization: Multi-language support (DE/EN)
* Admin Panel: Administrative functions for user roles and system management

# Technical Stack
* Frontend: Remix (React-based full-stack framework)
* Database: SQLite with Prisma ORM
* Search: Meilisearch
* Authentication: Keycloak
* File Storage: S3-compatible storage (MinIO)
* Styling: CSS Modules
* Internationalization: i18next